<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
<style>
  body { font-family: Arial, sans-serif; font-size: 11pt; margin: 40px; color: #111; }
  h1 { color: #c00; font-size: 18pt; border-bottom: 2px solid #c00; padding-bottom: 8px; }
  h2 { font-size: 13pt; color: #333; border-bottom: 1px solid #ccc; margin-top: 20px; }
  table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; margin: 12px 0; font-size: 10pt; }
  th { background: #1a1a1a; color: white; padding: 8px 10px; text-align: left; font-size: 9pt; }
  td { padding: 8px 10px; border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e5e5; }
  .critical { color: #c00; font-weight: bold; }
  .signature-box { background: #f5f5f5; border: 1px solid #ccc; padding: 14px;
                   font-family: monospace; font-size: 9pt; word-break: break-all; }
  .footer { margin-top: 30px; font-size: 9pt; color: #888; border-top: 1px solid #ccc; padding-top: 10px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<h1>CERT-In Cyber Incident Report</h1>
<p><strong>Reporting Organisation:</strong> {{ organisation_name }}<br>
<strong>Report ID:</strong> {{ report_id }}<br>
<strong>Generated:</strong> {{ generated_at }} UTC<br>
<strong>Regulatory Framework:</strong> CERT-In S.O. 1374(E) — 6-Hour Mandatory Reporting</p>

<h2>1. Incident Summary</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>Field</th><th>Value</th></tr>
  <tr><td>Incident Type</td><td>{{ incident_type }}</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Severity</td><td class="critical">{{ severity }}</td></tr>
  <tr><td>First Detected</td><td>{{ detection_time }}</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Indicator of Compromise</td><td><code>{{ indicator_value }}</code></td></tr>
  <tr><td>Indicator Type</td><td>{{ indicator_type }}</td></tr>
  <tr><td>QMind Lead Category</td><td>{{ lead_category }}</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Confidence Score</td><td>{{ confidence }}</td></tr>
  <tr><td>Detection Source</td><td>{{ source }}</td></tr>
</table>

<h2>2. Technical Description</h2>
<p>{{ description }}</p>

<h2>3. Affected Systems</h2>
<ul>{% for s in affected_systems %}<li>{{ s }}</li>{% else %}<li>Under investigation</li>{% endfor %}</ul>

<h2>4. MITRE ATT&CK Techniques</h2>
<ul>{% for t in mitre_techniques %}<li>{{ t }}</li>{% else %}<li>Mapping in progress</li>{% endfor %}</ul>

<h2>5. Recommended Remediation Actions</h2>
<ol>{% for a in recommended_actions %}<li>{{ a }}</li>{% else %}<li>Manual analyst review required</li>{% endfor %}</ol>

<h2>6. Cryptographic Attestation (Dilithium-3 / NIST FIPS 204)</h2>
<div class="signature-box">
<strong>Algorithm:</strong> Dilithium-3 (ML-DSA, NIST FIPS 204 Post-Quantum Digital Signature)<br>
<strong>Report Hash (SHA-256):</strong> {{ report_hash }}<br>
<strong>Signature:</strong> {{ signature_hex }}<br>
<strong>Key Reference:</strong> {{ pubkey_ref }}<br>
<strong>Signed At:</strong> {{ signed_at }} UTC
</div>

<div class="footer">
<strong>Submitter:</strong> Kebos AI — Pynevera Technologies<br>
<strong>Platform:</strong> Kebos AI v1.0 — Post-Quantum Native Security Operations Platform<br>
<strong>Compliance:</strong> CERT-In S.O. 1374(E) | DPDPA 2023 | RBI Cybersecurity Framework<br>
This report was auto-generated and cryptographically signed. The Dilithium-3 signature above
constitutes a valid digital attestation under Indian IT Act Section 5.
</div>
</body>
</html>
